WEBVTT

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.240
I'm Akechi Mitsuhide?

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:17.530
I killed...

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.580
I killed Nobunaga-sama!

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:01.100
Mitsuhide-san!

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.400
Mitsuhide-san...

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:50.300
Ranmaru!

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.020
Nobunaga-sama!

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.820
Amnesia?

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:00.760
Yes, when I found her,

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:03.560
she couldn't remember who she was.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:08.070
So, you decided to stay with her, huh?

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.520
I couldn't just leave her.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:13.350
And I wanted to keep a close eye on her.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:17.690
But when there was a 
fire not too long ago,

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:21.110
she saw the flames and slipped into a coma.

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:23.580
She didn't get up after that.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:27.680
I stayed with her and tried 
to keep an eye on her, but...

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:33.520
Where did Mitsuhide-san go?

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.350
<i>Everything...</i>

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.740
<i>I remember everything...</i>

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:52.410
<i>I... I killed Nobunaga-sama.</i>

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.760
I am truly honored

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.710
you answered the summons 
of my lord, Nobunaga.

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:02.500
Yoshiteru-sama.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:05.840
And Ieyasu-dono.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.670
Sessai-sensei, as a representative 
of the Imagawa clan.

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:12.030
And Kanetsugu-dono as a representative 
of the Uesugi Clan...

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:15.440
Mitsuhide, that's enough 
formal introductions.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:18.940
If we don't get started, 
the food will get cold.

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:23.840
Come on, hold out your 
cup and I'll pour.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:27.300
I'm actually the Shogun, you know.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.410
Sure, but that doesn't 
mean anything anymore.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:31.500
Come on.

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:34.710
I can't believe

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.890
Ieyasu-dono grew up to 
be such a fine general.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.610
I'd never have pegged you for it

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:43.360
when you were a hostage 
of the Imagawa Clan.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:47.350
You taught me a lot back then.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:48.470
Come to think of it,

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.000
you used to sing in the 
corner of the courtyard,

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.190
perhaps to forget the loneliness 
of being a hostage.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:56.480
Did she?

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:59.600
Yes, she was very good.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.030
I'd love to hear.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:06.070
No, I'm not good enough
to let other people hear me sing.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:10.240
Anyway, I've heard the rumors 
about you, Kanetsugu-san.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:13.820
That you're very, very 
loyal to Kenshin-san.

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:16.830
So you've heard?

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.530
Oh jeez, I'm embarrassed.

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:20.340
Um, everyone,

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:24.030
I'm terribly sorry, but I must be going.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:26.630
Do you have something you have to do?

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.510
Yes, I have some remaining work to tend to.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:32.180
Just do it tomorrow.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.150
Everybody's enjoying their drinks.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.980
Don't you think so, Yosshi?

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:38.850
Y-Yosshi—

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.360
I'm afraid I must insist.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:45.300
And everyone here is a 
famous person in our world,

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.360
including the Shogun herself.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:51.150
To those of us who do
not possess a secret treasure,

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:54.120
it bothers us to stay here.

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:56.630
Actually, we don't...

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:58.230
That's right, Mitsuhide-san.

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.880
Nobody cares.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:04.410
Mitsuhide, are you still 
upset about what happened?

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:07.470
No, not at all.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:10.070
What about you, monkey girl?

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:12.250
You don't have a treasure, either.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:15.820
Of course, I'll stay here till the end.

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:18.980
I can't leave all this food!

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:22.130
You're so silly, monkey girl.

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:25.990
Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.200
Mitsuhide-san...

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:38.130
Jeez... she's still grumpy about that.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.720
She's gonna go bald one of these days.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:44.360
Oh!

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:45.420
Ieyasu?

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:51.670
Did something happen with Mitsuhide-san?

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:54.270
N-Nothing really.

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:56.120
Just...

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.310
Just?

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:00.790
We got into an argument 
during a strategy session

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:02.350
and I got angry.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:07.170
Shut up and stop worrying 
about the details.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:09.090
Our next battle is the last thing
standing between us and total conquest.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:11.830
We must be extremely careful.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:14.910
Now see here, there's such a 
thing as momentum in war.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:16.730
It's fine to be careful, but

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:19.620
if we waste too much time, 
we'll lose our opportunity.

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.590
Which is why we should carefully prepare,

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:25.110
so that we don't squander that chance.

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:28.300
It's because you're 
such a petty stickler

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.630
that you'll never get a secret treasure.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:34.520
That has nothing to do with it!

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.100
No, it does.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.830
You've got plans, but no dreams.

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:40.370
No ambitions.

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:42.480
No drive!

00:07:50.890 --> 00:07:53.590
Why did you say that?

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:55.230
You know the fact that she doesn't

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:57.570
have a secret treasure bothers her.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:07:59.450
I couldn't help it.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.710
She picked a fight with me.

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:06.000
You should apologize to her.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:06.710
Why?

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:09.050
Nobunaga-san...

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:12.010
Why do I have to apologize?

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:15.220
She's my... retainer!

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:17.230
I have no reason to apologize.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:29.300
Here you go.

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:40.780
I love tea.

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:46.130
In a tea room, your wealth 
and rank mean nothing.

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:49.420
Nor does whether or not you 
have a secret treasure.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.960
No matter how talented 
people may think you are,

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:56.150
without a secret treasure,

00:08:56.150 --> 00:09:00.080
this world doesn't accept 
you as somebody.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:05.020
You shouldn't worry too much 
about the secret treasures.

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:11.980
A secret treasure is a physical 
manifestation of great power.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:15.740
To some, it is ambition.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.360
A drive to master something.

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:19.990
To others, it's karma.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:25.100
There are painters and poets 
with secret treasures,

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:27.480
so if I continue to 
master the art of tea,

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:30.750
perhaps I'll attain one someday.

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:36.380
But even if I did, 
would that make me happy?

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:42.120
Strong emotions make people strong.

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:46.540
But they make them suffer, as well.

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:50.640
Sometimes I feel that way...

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:55.290
I'm sorry. I must be boring you.

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:56.220
Not at all.

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:05.910
Rikyuu, I'm thirsty.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:09.040
Get me some tea. Now.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.850
Yes, immediately.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:20.850
Here you go.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.610
Bitter!

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:27.910
Another.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:28.840
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.230
Nobunaga-sama!

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.690
Nobunaga-sama!

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:37.570
Ranmaru, I'm here.

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:41.480
Nobunaga-sama,
Hideyoshi-san has something

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.450
she needs to talk to 
you about immediately.

00:10:44.090 --> 00:10:46.330
Okay. I'll be right there.

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:56.280
My, my...

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:58.470
She's like a whirlwind.

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:01.720
If somebody doesn't keep 
a close hold on her,

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:04.720
she'll blow off somewhere.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.470
Is there anyone

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:12.980
who can hold onto Nobunaga-sama?

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.910
Hideyoshi-sama got a secret treasure?

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:30.610
She's been winning lots of glory lately,

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:34.690
and they say perhaps
she's grown up as a person.

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:40.690
They also say her secret treasure surpasses Ieyasu-sama's and rivals Nobunaga-sama's!

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:49.150
Here.

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:55.060
Um...

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:56.070
Your tea...

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:06.060
<i>Ever since I heard that Hideyoshi 
got a secret treasure,</i>

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:08.490
<i>my days of pain began.</i>

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:12.870
<i>Her smile was like the rising sun.</i>

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:18.670
<i>Whenever she was nearby, 
Nobunaga-sama was always smiling.</i>

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:23.680
<i>Jealousy. Pure jealousy.</i>

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:29.270
<i>Those dark feelings flooded my heart.</i>

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:32.320
<i>And then, one day...</i>

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:50.370
<i>What is this feeling?</i>

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:55.620
<i>Something...</i>

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:58.520
<i>Something is inside me.</i>

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:04.890
<i>Thinking back, perhaps it was 
the seed of a secret treasure.</i>

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:09.790
<i>I was jealous of Nobunaga-sama's 
sworn friend, Ieyasu-dono.</i>

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:13.400
<i>And jealous of how Hideyoshi 
received her love.</i>

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:16.640
<i>I was jealous of all those
who had a secret treasure.</i>

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:20.300
<i>Nonetheless, negative power is still power.</i>

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:24.880
<i>Those strong emotions fed it, 
and it grew by the instant.</i>

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.070
<i>It started to throb powerfully.</i>

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:33.080
<i>My secret treasure, growing by 
feeding on my dark feelings.</i>

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:36.380
<i>How awful... How terrible...</i>

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:38.080
<i>However,</i>

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:41.770
<i>strangely, I loved it still.</i>

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:50.640
Mitsuhide-san, you've seemed tired lately. You should get some rest.

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:53.560
Thank you for your concern.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:56.080
But our next battle is the final one,

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:58.190
before we finish conquering.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:00.060
There are many preparations to be made.

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:03.870
As someone who'll soon be in charge 
of the expeditionary force,

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:06.070
I cannot take the time to rest.

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:10.360
And if I can win glory in this battle,

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:14.240
then Nobunaga-sama will accept 
me as someone of worth.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.370
And then I'm sure...

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:22.130
<i>And then the day arrived.</i>

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:27.380
N-Nobunaga-sama?

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:28.790
What did you say?

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:31.010
You didn't hear me?

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:34.750
Hideyoshi will command 
the expeditionary force.

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:39.190
But I was to be in charge—

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:40.900
I changed my mind.

00:14:41.410 --> 00:14:43.080
No...

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:43.940
That's all.

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:45.800
The conference is over.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:48.640
Please wait.

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:51.740
At least... at least tell me why!

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:52.990
Nobunaga-sama.

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:54.990
Mitsuhide-san, calm down!

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:58.110
Please, Mitsuhide-san, calm down!

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:56.710
Nobunaga-sama...

00:14:58.110 --> 00:14:59.460
Nobunaga-sama!

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:09.180
Hideyoshi-san has left safely, it seems.

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:10.070
Yes.

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:17.280
Why did you put her in charge?

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:22.060
Weren't you planning on
giving it to Mitsuhide-san?

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:28.070
Are you still mad at what happened?

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.390
No.

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:31.280
Then, why?

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:34.560
I wanted to keep her near me.

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:38.880
Once this battle is over,

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:41.150
my conquest is as good as finished.

00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:43.890
At last, my dream will come true.

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:48.360
It's something I've desired forever.

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:51.850
But now that it's almost here...

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:55.530
You're scared, aren't you?

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.030
Don't be stupid.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:02.310
I'm just... feeling a little uneasy.

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:05.410
I don't know why.

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:08.910
I see.

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:11.840
So you want the person 
you trust the most,

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:14.030
Mitsuhide-san, by your side.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:19.060
Then you should just tell her.

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:21.160
I can't tell her that.

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:24.410
Listen, this is a secret!

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:26.880
You cannot, must not, tell her!

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:44.220
Why?

00:16:45.140 --> 00:16:48.690
Why did Nobunaga-sama
choose Hideyoshi over me?

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:52.240
Why, Nobunaga-sama?

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:08.630
"If the cuckoo won't sing, kill it."

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.460
Mitsuhide-san?

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:19.160
Rikyuu-san?

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:24.080
Mitsuhide-san?

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:30.250
Mitsuhide-san...

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:33.470
Rikyuu-san.

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:38.020
I'm sorry for the trouble.

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:40.330
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:42.430
You and I are friends.

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:45.320
But what were you doing out there?

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:49.300
It seems I'd lost my memories.

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:51.030
Your memories?

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:55.940
I think it's because I couldn't 
bear to admit what I'd done.

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:59.860
But now... I remember it all.

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:02.910
With my own hands, I...

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:06.790
Mitsuhide-san, you don't know do you?

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:13.030
Nobunaga-sama is alive.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:18.260
I see.

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:22.920
And so she's trying to 
return to our world...

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:26.070
Yes. She's as pushy as ever,

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:28.230
grabbing all the treasures she can find.

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.020
N-Nobunaga-sama.

00:19:33.390 --> 00:19:35.420
What brings you here?

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:38.710
What else? The secret treasure.

00:19:38.710 --> 00:19:42.910
But nobody here has...

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:44.280
You can't hide it from me.

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:46.300
Wait!

00:19:53.620 --> 00:19:55.130
Nobunaga-sama...

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:56.990
Mitsuhide...

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:00.380
I'm surprised.

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:04.610
I didn't think the secret 
treasure I came for was yours.

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:08.370
Well, if you've got the 
guts to kill your lord,

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:10.970
then I suppose it makes 
sense you'd have one.

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:15.640
Whatever.

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:19.590
It'll get me another secret treasure.

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:27.450
So you're prepared for this, then.

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:30.640
It won't allow me to atone,

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:32.150
but if my secret treasure

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:35.700
will be of use to you, I offer it gladly.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:51.850
I'm taking your secret treasure.

00:20:53.010 --> 00:20:54.060
<i>This is for the best.</i>

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:02.600
<i>My secret treasure, 
filled with its dark emotions,</i>

00:21:02.600 --> 00:21:04.270
<i>can be of use to her...</i>

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:09.950
<i>If it can help her get home,</i>

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:18.050
<i>and even if this means goodbye 
forever, that's okay.</i>

00:21:29.970 --> 00:21:32.640
Mitsuhide, you need to 
know when to give up!

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:34.580
I'm sorry.

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:40.480
But... But... I can't give this to you!

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:43.610
Wait!

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:46.160
Move.

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:47.130
I won't.

00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:50.030
Rikyuu, you...

00:21:52.050 --> 00:21:55.330
If you interfere, I can't 
guarantee you'll live.

00:21:56.310 --> 00:21:58.740
Mitsuhide-san is a dear friend

00:21:58.740 --> 00:22:01.170
and a fellow student in the way of tea.

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:06.630
And I'm prepared to sacrifice 
my life for her!

00:23:46.400 --> 00:23:48.510
Next is Takeda Shingen,

00:23:48.510 --> 00:23:51.050
the Cavalry Queen who even 
Nobunaga-sama feared.

